# RFC 8288 Link headers — site-wide discovery pointers to resources that are
# genuinely the same on every page (sitemap, the RFC 9727 API catalog, the
# OpenAPI spec). Per-page pointers (e.g. an atom page's own markdown twin)
# are NOT here: Cloudflare Pages' _headers format can't template a per-path
# value into a header, and hand-writing one block per atom page (474 of
# them) would be an unmaintainable duplicate of the URL structure already
# expressed correctly in the sitemap and each page's own <head>. Those use a
# real <link rel="alternate"> tag instead — see generate_atom_pages.py.
/*
  Link: <https://a2uicatalog.ai/sitemap.xml>; rel="sitemap", <https://a2uicatalog.ai/.well-known/api-catalog>; rel="service-desc"; type="application/linkset+json", <https://a2uicatalog.ai/openapi.json>; rel="service-desc"; type="application/json"

/
  Link: <https://a2uicatalog.ai/index.md>; rel="alternate"; type="text/markdown"

# Diagram Studio MCP App (2026-09-20): the view is fetched by the MCP Worker, and its D2 engine (a gzip, since Cloudflare static
# assets cap one file at 25 MiB) is fetched by the view itself from inside a host's sandboxed iframe, a different origin, so it
# needs CORS. Public, unauthenticated, read-only static files.
/surfaces/diagram-studio/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Amiga MCP App (2026-09-22): same reasoning as diagram-studio above, and the same fix was needed for the same reason -- the view's
# own HTML is fetched by reference by the MCP Worker, but vAmigaWeb (the emulator) itself fetches ALL its own assets (vAmiga.wasm,
# js/*, roms/*, sounds/*, game.adf) from inside the host's sandboxed iframe, a different origin, which needs CORS on every one of
# them. Found live, 2026-09-22 (Curtis: black screen; console showed "No 'Access-Control-Allow-Origin' header is present" on
# vAmiga.wasm itself -- the WASM module cannot load at all without this, which is why nothing booted, not even the toolbar).
/surfaces/amiga/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# brick_build_3d part meshes (spec/brick-parts-v0.1.md): fetched by reference from inside the host's sandboxed
# MCP Apps iframe, a different origin, same reasoning as diagram-studio and amiga above. Long cache: baked meshes
# only change when the curated part set or the LDraw pin changes (ldraw-parts-build), which recommits the whole set.
/parts/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, immutable
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
